- **Green (batch-owned):** `proof-layout.mjs` on the nineteen items: 98 steps, 0 defects; `precheck.mts` on the sixteen proof-bearing items: 16 checked, 0 failing; `rendercheck.mjs` on nineteen items + two pages: OK; `content-policy.mjs <batch-9 manifest>` (item mode): 19 items, 0 errors, 0 warnings; `proof-contract.mjs --strict`: 19/19 checked, 0 errors, 0 warnings; `coverage-checklist.mjs --require-destination`: 55 harvested results, 0 errors, 0 warnings; `manifest-deps.mjs` on the batch manifest: 19 items, 0 errors; `depcheck.mjs`: no finding (of any code) names a batch-9 item or page — the command exits 1 only on unrelated published/legacy states elsewhere in the workspace.
- **`item-dependency-levels.mjs check --run`**: exits 1 with 144 `empty scaffold inventory` errors, all for other concurrent batches whose manifests are not transcribed; no error mentions `cm-math-rigid` or `cm-math-rigid-examples`, so batch-9 labels are computed-consistent.
- **`content-policy.mjs --manifest-only`**: reports `batch-item-already-exists` for all nineteen ids, because plan-spec pages carry empty `items` arrays and manifest-only mode reads the plan as a future minting batch while the item files already exist. This is the known mechanical state recorded by sibling batches; item mode is green and the engine's Step-1 splice is the intended resolution. The shared plan was not edited by hand.
- **`validate-plan.mjs research/plan-spec.json --run ...`**: exits 1. For the A page it reports two warning-class `redundant-prereq` rows (`the-lebesgue-integral-and-the-convergence-theorems` is required directly and also reached through `cm-math-balances` and through `cm-math-geometry`) and six hard `[undeclared-prereq]` errors: items depend on the root pages `sigma-algebras-and-borel-sets`, `measures-and-their-basic-properties`, `gaussian-elimination-and-row-reduction`, `the-exponential-function`, `sine-cosine-and-the-definition-of-pi`, `the-logarithm-and-general-powers`, outside the closure of the plan-seeded four-entry `requires`. These are real transitive root-page homes of used published suppliers (`def-borel-sigma-algebra`, `def-measure`, `thm-invertible-matrix-theorem`, `cor-exponential-is-a-bijection-onto-positive-reals`, `def-sine-and-cosine-by-power-series`, `thm-derivative-of-exponential`, `thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral`), so the finding is not removable by dropping dependencies without making the proofs unsound. The B page initially failed to mirror the plan's five-entry `requires` (only `cm-math-rigid` was listed, producing four `undeclared-prereq` errors for the four root pages); the manifest and page carrier were corrected to mirror plan-spec verbatim (repair 6 above), and the repaired check reports no B-page finding. Resolution of the remaining six A-page findings is an owner/adjudicator decision — either extend the page `requires` (manifest first, then plan, via the documented splice gate) or license reading-order access to published root pages without `requires` entries. This batch did not edit the shared plan; the A-page manifest still mirrors the plan-seeded list. Concurrent batches (e.g. `cm-math-central`, which reports 15 findings in the same check) show the same class, confirming it is run-wide.
